H. MQL5 runtime configuration

Standard MQL5 "input" variables are normally initialisation parameters. Changing a stored input value remotely does not automatically change the native input variable of a running EA.

Build a separate runtime configuration layer.

The EA must initialise runtime values from its standard inputs and then use validated active runtime values for all relevant strategy calculations.

For example:

- InitialLotSize.
- ActiveLotSize.
- InitialStopLoss.
- ActiveStopLoss.
- InitialTakeProfit.
- ActiveTakeProfit.

Refactor the existing EA carefully so the strategy reads the appropriate active configuration.

Do not rewrite the existing trading strategy unnecessarily.

Inspect the original source before modifying it.

Some inputs may require controlled EA reinitialisation. Mark these accurately.

If a setting cannot safely change while positions are open, delay application or require the appropriate safe procedure.

Existing position management must remain operational during configuration changes.

