Risk controls must exist at two levels:

1. Account-wide.
2. Individual EA installation.

Account-wide controls take precedence.

Support:

- Maximum daily loss.
- Maximum total exposure.
- Maximum lot size.
- Maximum open positions.
- Maximum trades per day.
- Maximum spread.
- Minimum margin level.
- Trading sessions.
- Allowed instruments.
- Emergency stop policy.

Where multiple EAs operate on one MT5 account, aggregate risk must be checked.

Prevent one EA from exceeding the account-wide risk budget because another EA is also trading.

EA-specific settings cannot override account-wide protections.

Never automatically close all open positions when an emergency stop is requested unless the customer has explicitly selected and confirmed a supported close-position policy.

Default pause behaviour should block new entries while allowing the EA to manage existing positions safely.

