13. REMOTE EA CONTROL

Provide controls:

- Pause.
- Resume.
- Stop.
- Emergency stop.

Define their meaning clearly.

Pause:
Block new entries while continuing safe management of existing positions.

Resume:
Allow new entries only when account and EA safeguards permit.

Stop:
Disable new entries and follow the explicitly defined existing-position policy.

Emergency stop:
Execute the configured emergency policy. Do not assume this means close every open trade.

Commands must be versioned, authenticated, time-limited and acknowledged.

Command states:

- Pending.
- Delivered.
- Applied.
- Rejected.
- Expired.
- Failed.

If an EA is offline, show that the command is waiting.

Never claim that a command was applied without EA acknowledgement.

