29. IMPORTANT IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS

Do not replace the real backend with hardcoded demo data without labelling it.

Do not create buttons that appear functional but have no action.

Do not show successful installation until the installation agent or EA confirms it.

Do not show an EA as running without actual runtime confirmation.

Do not display remote configuration as applied before acknowledgement.

Do not allow configuration changes to bypass risk limits.

Do not assume all EAs have identical inputs.

Do not assume every MT5 broker uses the same XAUUSD symbol name. Support broker-specific symbols and symbol mapping.

Do not assume every EA can run simultaneously on the same account.

Do not rewrite the existing EA trading strategy when integrating the bridge.

Do not create duplicate MQL5 event handlers.

Do not put broker passwords in ordinary Android storage or backend database fields.

Keep demo and live environments strictly separated.

All external services must be configurable through environment variables and secure configuration.

Use clean architecture, reusable components, modular code and production-oriented error handling.

